WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:06.425
robots.txt, sitemaps and redirects: the small files that steer search engines.

2
00:00:07.925 --> 00:00:12.533
What each file tells a crawler, the rules that trip people up, how to block

3
00:00:12.533 --> 00:00:16.096
AI crawlers, and how to move pages without losing traffic.

4
00:00:17.496 --> 00:00:21.039
robots.txt: a polite request to crawlers.

5
00:00:21.039 --> 00:00:27.693
robots.txt sits at the root of your site, for example example.com/robots.txt.

6
00:00:28.993 --> 00:00:31.883
Sitemaps: a list of pages you want found.

7
00:00:31.883 --> 00:00:37.099
An XML sitemap lists the pages you want search engines to know about, each

8
00:00:37.099 --> 00:00:40.129
in a loc tag with an optional lastmod date.

9
00:00:41.429 --> 00:00:44.316
Redirects: moving pages without losing visitors.

10
00:00:44.316 --> 00:00:48.586
When a page moves, the old address should answer with a redirect to the

11
00:00:48.586 --> 00:00:49.067
new one.

12
00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:54.356
Check the page itself. Once the files are in place, check the pages.

13
00:00:55.656 --> 00:00:59.860
To try it, open robots.txt Generator & Tester in OpenFile.

14
00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:03.991
Drop in a file, adjust the settings and press the button.

15
00:01:03.991 --> 00:01:07.688
It all runs on your device, so nothing is uploaded.

16
00:01:09.388 --> 00:01:12.993
Read the full post, with live demos, on the OpenFile blog.
